> ecartis@digitalkingdom.org writes:
> > Also, are there suggested/official lujvo/gismu for the days of the month?
> > If not, I propose the following: Since {pavdei} is "Monday" and etc.,
>
> While I agree that "pavdei" should be 'Monday', my understanding is that
> this is controversial, with the other view asserting that it should be
> 'Sunday'. Last I heard, there was no consensus on this.

As I understand it, some people begin the week on Sunday and others on Monday. 
We can have the same names for six days of the week by using {zeldei} or 
(nondei} for Sunday. But that leaves the Seventh-day Adventists with 
{xavdei}.

I can see a trace of the controversy in Russian. Вторник, четверг, and пятница 
indicate that Monday is day one, but среда indicates that Wednesday is the 
middle day.

Pierre


